&lt;encodingType&gt;The name of the bucket.&lt;/encodingType&gt;
&lt;delimiter&gt;images&lt;/delimiter&gt;
&lt;/listObjects&gt;
</code></pre> getBucketLifecycleConfiguration<p>The getBucketLifecycleConfiguration operation returns the lifecycle configuration information set on the bucket. To use this operation, permissions should be given to perform the s3:GetLifecycleConfiguration action. The bucket owner has this permission by default and can grant this permission to others. There is usually some time lag before lifecycle configuration deletion is fully propagated to all the Amazon S3 systems. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required bucketName The name of the bucket. Yes responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazons3.getBucketLifecycleConfiguration&gt;
