&lt;/getBucketPolicy&gt;
</code></pre> listObjectVersions<p>The listObjectVersions operation lists metadata about all of the versions of objects in a bucket. Request parameters can be used as selection criteria to return metadata about a subset of all the object versions. To use this operation, the user must have READ access to the bucket. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required bucketName The name of the bucket. Yes delimiter A delimiter is a character used to group keys. Optional encodingType Requests Amazon S3 to encode the response and specifies the encoding method to use. Optional keyMarker Specifies the key in the bucket that you want to start listing from. See also versionIdMarker below. Optional maxKeys Sets the maximum number of keys returned in the response body. Optional prefix Limits the response to keys that begin with the specified prefix. Optional versionIdMarker Specifies the object version you want to start listing from. Optional responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazons3.listObjectVersions&gt;
