receiveMessage<p>This operation retrieves one or more messages, with a maximum limit of 10 messages, from the specified queue. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue to which a message is sent. Yes messageSystemAttributeNames A list of attributes that need to be returned along with each message. The attribute should be separated by ','. <code>Eg:  'SenderId, SentTimestamp'</code>. No maxNumberOfMessages The maximum number of messages to return. No messageAttributeNames The names of the message attributes. The attributes should be separated by ','. <code>Eg:  'attributeName1, attributeName2'</code> No visibilityTimeout The duration (in seconds) that the received messages are hidden from subsequent retrieve requests after being retrieved by a ReceiveMessage request. No waitTimeSeconds The duration (in seconds) for which the call will wait for a message to arrive in the queue before returning. No apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.receiveMessage configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;maxNumberOfMessages&gt;{$ctx:maxNumberOfMessages}&lt;/maxNumberOfMessages&gt;
&lt;waitTimeSeconds&gt;{$ctx:waitTimeSeconds}&lt;/waitTimeSeconds&gt;
&lt;messageAttributeNames&gt;{$ctx:messageAttributeNames}&lt;/messageAttributeNames&gt;
&lt;messageSystemAttributeNames&gt;{$ctx:messageSystemAttributeNames}&lt;/messageSystemAttributeNames&gt;
&lt;visibilityTimeout&gt;{$ctx:visibilityTimeout}&lt;/visibilityTimeout&gt;
&lt;attributes&gt;{$ctx:attributes}&lt;/attributes&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.receiveMessage&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.receiveMessage configKey="AMAZON_SQS_CONNECTION"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;https://sqs.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/844234390511/Queue&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;maxNumberOfMessages&gt;5&lt;/maxNumberOfMessages&gt;
&lt;waitTimeSeconds&gt;5&lt;/waitTimeSeconds&gt;
&lt;messageAttributeNames&gt;attributeName1, attributeName2&lt;/messageAttributeNames&gt;
&lt;messageSystemAttributeNames&gt;SenderId, SentTimestamp&lt;/messageSystemAttributeNames&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.receiveMessage&gt;
</code></pre> sendMessage<p>This operation delivers a message to the specified queue. You can send payload messages up to 256 KB (262,144 bytes) in size. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue to which a message is sent. Yes messageBody The message to be sent, a String that is a maximum of 256 KB in size. Yes delaySeconds The number of seconds (0 to 900, which is 15 minutes) to delay a specific message. No messageAttributes The message attributes to send. The value should be a string in JSON format.<code>Eg: { 'attributeName' : { 'DataType': 'value', 'StringValue': 'value' }}</code>" No messageDeduplicationId The ID of the message deduplication. This parameter applies only to FIFO (first-in-first-out) queues No messageGroupId The ID of the message group. This parameter applies only to FIFO (first-in-first-out) queues No messageSystemAttributes The message system attributes to send. The value should be a string in JSON format.<code>Eg:{ 'systemAttributeName' :{ 'DataType': 'value', 'StringValue': 'value' } }</code> No apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.sendMessage configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;messageBody&gt;{$ctx:messageBody}&lt;/messageBody&gt;
&lt;delaySeconds&gt;{$ctx:delaySeconds}&lt;/delaySeconds&gt;
&lt;messageAttributes&gt;{$ctx:messageAttributes}&lt;/messageAttributes&gt;
&lt;messageSystemAttributes&gt;{$ctx:messageSystemAttributes}&lt;/messageSystemAttributes&gt;
&lt;messageDeduplicationId&gt;{$ctx:messageDeduplicationId}&lt;/messageDeduplicationId&gt;
&lt;messageGroupId&gt;{$ctx:messageGroupId}&lt;/messageGroupId&gt;  &lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.sendMessage&gt; </code></pre> <p>Sample request for sendMessage</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.sendMessage&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;https://sqs.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/882234390511/Queue&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;messageBody&gt;Hi&lt;/messageBody&gt;
&lt;delaySeconds&gt;5&lt;/delaySeconds&gt;
&lt;messageAttributes&gt;"{ 'attributeName' : { 'DataType': 'value', 'StringValue': 'value' }}"&lt;/messageAttributes&gt;
&lt;messageSystemAttributes&gt;"{ 'systemAttributeName' :{ 'DataType': 'value', 'StringValue': 'value' } }"&lt;/messageSystemAttributes&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.sendMessage&gt;
</code></pre> sendMessageBatch<p>This operation delivers batch messages to the specified queue. You can send payload messages up to 256 KB (262,144 bytes) in size. See the related API documentation for more information.  queueUrl The URL of the queue to which a message is sent. Yes messageRequestEntries The list of messages to be sent, a String that is a maximum of 256 KB in size. <code>Eg: [{'delaySeconds': 0, 'id': 'id1', 'messageBody': 'hi', 'messageAttributes': {'my_attribute_name_1': {'DataType': 'String','StringValue': 'my_attribute_value_1'}}, messageSystemAttributes: {'AWSTraceHeader': {'DataType': 'String','StringValue': 'AWS X-Ray'}}}]</code> Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.sendMessageBatch configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;messageRequestEntries&gt;{$ctx:messageRequestEntries}&lt;/messageRequestEntries&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.sendMessageBatch&gt; </code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.sendMessageBatch configKey="AMAZON_SQS_CONNECTION"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;https://sqs.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/882234390511/Queue&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;messageRequestEntries&gt;[{delaySeconds: 0, id: id1, messageBody: hi, messageAttributes: {"my_attribute_name_1": {"DataType": "String","StringValue": "my_attribute_value_1"}}, messageSystemAttributes: {"AWSTraceHeader": {"DataType": "String","StringValue": "AWS X-Ray"}}}]&lt;/messageRequestEntries&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.sendMessageBatch&gt;
</code></pre> deleteMessage<p>This operation deletes the specified message from the specified queue. You specify the message by using the message's receipt handle and not the message ID you received when you sent the message. Even if the message is locked by another reader due to the visibility timeout setting, it is still deleted from the queue. If you leave a message in the queue for longer than the queue's configured retention period, Amazon SQS automatically deletes it. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue from which messages are deleted. Yes receiptHandle The receipt handle associated with the message to be deleted. Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.deleteMessage configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;receiptHandle&gt;{$ctx:receiptHandle}&lt;/receiptHandle&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.deleteMessage&gt; </code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.deleteMessage configKey="AMAZON_SQS_CONNECTION"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;https://sqs.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/882234390511/Queue&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;receiptHandle&gt;2432435435645654656567&lt;/receiptHandle&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.deleteMessage&gt; </code></pre> deleteMessageBatch<p>This operation deletes multiple messages from the specified queue. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue from which messages are deleted. Yes messageRequestEntries A list of receipt handles for the messages to be deleted.<code>Eg: [{'receiptHandle': '122324343', 'id': 'id1' }]</code> Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.deleteMessageBatch configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;messageRequestEntries&gt;{$ctx:messageRequestEntries}&lt;/messageRequestEntries&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.deleteMessageBatch&gt; </code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.deleteMessageBatch configKey="AMAZON_SQS_CONNECTION"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;https://sqs.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/882234390511/Queue&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;messageRequestEntries&gt;{$ctx:messageRequestEntries}&lt;/messageRequestEntries&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.deleteMessageBatch&gt;   </code></pre> changeMessageVisibility<p>This operation changes the visibility timeout of a specified message in a queue to a new value. See the Visibility Timeout in the Amazon SQS Developer Guide).  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue whose message's visibility is changed Yes receiptHandle The receipt handle associated with the message, whose visibility timeout is changed. Yes visibilityTimeout The new value (in seconds - from 0 to 43200 - maximum 12 hours) for the message's visibility timeout. Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.changeMessageVisibility configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;  &lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;receiptHandle&gt;{$ctx:receiptHandle}&lt;/receiptHandle&gt;
&lt;visibilityTimeout&gt;{$ctx:visibilityTimeout}&lt;/visibilityTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.changeMessageVisibility&gt; </code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.changeMessageVisibility configKey="AMAZON_SQS_CONNECTION"&gt;  &lt;queueUrl&gt;https://sqs.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/882234390511/Queue&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;receiptHandle&gt;21321423453543556&lt;/receiptHandle&gt;
&lt;visibilityTimeout&gt;15&lt;/visibilityTimeout&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.changeMessageVisibility&gt;   </code></pre> changeMessageVisibilityBatch<p>This operation changes the visibility timeout of multiple messages. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue whose messages' visibility is changed Yes messageRequestEntries A list of receipt handles of the messages for which the visibility timeout must be changed. <code>Eg: [{'receiptHandle': '123234343434454', 'id': 'id1'', 'VisibilityTimeout': 5}]</code> Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.changeMessageVisibilityBatch configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;messageRequestEntries&gt;{$ctx:messageRequestEntries}&lt;/messageRequestEntries&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.changeMessageVisibilityBatch&gt; </code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.changeMessageVisibilityBatch configKey="AMAZON_SQS_CONNECTION"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;https://sqs.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/882234390511/Queue&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;messageRequestEntries&gt;[{'receiptHandle': '122324343', 'id': 'id1', 'VisibilityTimeout': 5 }]&lt;/messageRequestEntries&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.changeMessageVisibilityBatch&gt; </code></pre>

addPermission<p>This operation adds a permission to a queue for a specific principal. This allows sharing access to the queue. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue to which permissions are added. Yes awsAccountNumbers The AWS account numbers of the principal who will be given permission. The account ids should be separated by ','. <code>Eg: 111111111234, 111111111111</code> Yes actionNames The actions the client wants to allow for the specified principal. The actions should be separated by ','. <code>Eg: SendMessage, DeleteMessage</code> Yes label The unique identification of the permission you're setting. Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.addPermission configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;awsAccountNumbers&gt;{$ctx:awsAccountNumbers}&lt;/awsAccountNumbers&gt;
&lt;actionNames&gt;{$ctx:actionNames}&lt;/actionNames&gt;
&lt;label&gt;{$ctx:label}&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.addPermission&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.addPermission configKey="AMAZON_SQS_CONNECTION"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;https://sqs.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/882234390511/Queue&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;awsAccountNumbers&gt;844783390511, 111111111111&lt;/awsAccountNumbers&gt;
&lt;actionNames&gt;SendMessage, DeleteMessage&lt;/actionNames&gt;
&lt;label&gt;test&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.addPermission&gt;
</code></pre> removePermission<p>This operation revokes any permissions in the queue policy that matches the specified label. This allows sharing access to the queue. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue from which permissions are removed. Yes label The identification of the permission to remove Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.removePermission configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
