receiveMessage<p>This operation retrieves one or more messages, with a maximum limit of 10 messages, from the specified queue. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue to which a message is sent. Yes messageSystemAttributeNames A list of attributes that need to be returned along with each message. The attribute should be separated by ','. <code>Eg:  'SenderId, SentTimestamp'</code>. No maxNumberOfMessages The maximum number of messages to return. No messageAttributeNames The names of the message attributes. The attributes should be separated by ','. <code>Eg:  'attributeName1, attributeName2'</code> No visibilityTimeout The duration (in seconds) that the received messages are hidden from subsequent retrieve requests after being retrieved by a ReceiveMessage request. No waitTimeSeconds The duration (in seconds) for which the call will wait for a message to arrive in the queue before returning. No apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.receiveMessage configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
