&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;amazonsqs_operation_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.receiveMessage&gt;
</code></pre> sendMessage<p>This operation delivers a message to the specified queue. You can send payload messages up to 256 KB (262,144 bytes) in size. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue to which a message is sent. Yes messageBody The message to be sent, a String that is a maximum of 256 KB in size. Yes delaySeconds The number of seconds (0 to 900, which is 15 minutes) to delay a specific message. No messageAttributes The message attributes to send. The value should be a string in JSON format.<code>Eg: { 'attributeName' : { 'DataType': 'value', 'StringValue': 'value' }}</code>" No messageDeduplicationId The ID of the message deduplication. This parameter applies only to FIFO (first-in-first-out) queues No messageGroupId The ID of the message group. This parameter applies only to FIFO (first-in-first-out) queues No messageSystemAttributes The message system attributes to send. The value should be a string in JSON format.<code>Eg:{ 'systemAttributeName' :{ 'DataType': 'value', 'StringValue': 'value' } }</code> No apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.sendMessage configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
