&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.sendMessageBatch&gt; </code></pre> deleteMessage<p>This operation deletes the specified message from the specified queue. You specify the message by using the message's receipt handle and not the message ID you received when you sent the message. Even if the message is locked by another reader due to the visibility timeout setting, it is still deleted from the queue. If you leave a message in the queue for longer than the queue's configured retention period, Amazon SQS automatically deletes it. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue from which messages are deleted. Yes receiptHandle The receipt handle associated with the message to be deleted. Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.deleteMessage configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
