&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.deleteMessage&gt; </code></pre> deleteMessageBatch<p>This operation deletes multiple messages from the specified queue. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue from which messages are deleted. Yes messageRequestEntries A list of receipt handles for the messages to be deleted.<code>Eg: [{'receiptHandle': '122324343', 'id': 'id1' }]</code> Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.deleteMessageBatch configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
