&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;amazonsqs_operation_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.createQueue&gt;
</code></pre> deleteQueue<p>This operation deletes the queue specified by <code>QueueUrl</code>. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue to delete. Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.deleteQueue configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;amazonsqs_operation_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.deleteQueue&gt;
</code></pre> setQueueAttributes<p>This operation sets the value of one or more queue attributes, like a policy. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue whose attributes are set. Yes attributeEntries A map of attributes with their corresponding values. The value should be a string in JSON format. <code>Eg: {'RedrivePolicy': {'deadLetterTargetArn': 'arn:aws:sqs:us-east-1:884783870511:TestQueue', 'maxReceiveCount': 10}}</code> Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.setQueueAttributes configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;attributeEntries&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/attributeEntries&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;amazonsqs_operation_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.setQueueAttributes&gt;
</code></pre> getQueueAttributes<p>This operation gets attributes for the specified queue. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of the queue whose attribute information is retrieved. Yes attributes A list of attributes to retrieve information for. Default value is <code>All</code>. Each attribute must be listed in the string in a comma-separated format. <code>Eg: 'Policy', 'DelaySeconds'</code> No apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.getQueueAttributes configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;attributes&gt;{$ctx:attributes}&lt;/attributes&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;amazonsqs_operation_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.getQueueAttributes&gt;
</code></pre> getQueueUrl<p>This operation returns the URL of an existing queue. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueName The name of the queue. Yes accountId The AWS account ID without hyphens of the account that created the queue. Yes apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.getQueueUrl configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueName&gt;{$ctx:queueName}&lt;/queueName&gt;
&lt;accountId&gt;{$ctx:accountId}&lt;/accountId&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;amazonsqs_operation_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.getQueueUrl&gt;
</code></pre> listDeadLetterSourceQueues<p>This operation returns a list of the queues that have the <code>RedrivePolicy</code> queue attribute configured with a dead-letter queue. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueUrl The URL of a dead-letter queue. Yes maxResults Maximum number of results to include in the response. No nextToken Pagination token to request the next set of results. No apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.listDeadLetterSourceQueues configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueUrl&gt;{$ctx:queueUrl}&lt;/queueUrl&gt;
&lt;maxResults&gt;{$ctx:maxResults}&lt;/maxResults&gt;
&lt;nextToken&gt;{$ctx:nextToken}&lt;/nextToken&gt;
&lt;apiCallTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallTimeout}&lt;/apiCallTimeout&gt;
&lt;apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;{$ctx:apiCallAttemptTimeout}&lt;/apiCallAttemptTimeout&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;amazonsqs_operation_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/amazonsqs.listDeadLetterSourceQueues&gt;
</code></pre> listQueues<p>This operation returns a list of the queues in the current region. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required queueNamePrefix A string to use for filtering the list results. No maxResults Maximum number of results to include in the response. No nextToken Pagination token to request the next set of results. No apiCallTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to allow the client to complete the execution of an API call. No apiCallAttemptTimeout The amount of time(in seconds) to wait for the http request to complete before giving up and timing out. No responseVariable Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. Yes overwriteBody Replace the Message Body in Message Context with the output of the operation (This will remove the payload from the above variable). Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;amazonsqs.listQueues configKey="CONNECTION_NAME"&gt;
&lt;queueNamePrefix&gt;{$ctx:queueNamePrefix}&lt;/queueNamePrefix&gt;
