</code></pre>

call<p>The call operation can be used to access a program in the AS400 server.  Parameter Name Description Required programName The name of the program that you need to call. Yes. pcmlFileLocation The location of the file in the registry. Yes. pcmlInputs The XML representation of the input parameters for the program. Yes. pool.returnPoolName The name of the pool to which the AS400 connection should be returned to once the program call is finished. Yes. </p> <p>Sample configurations</p> <p><pre><code>&lt;pcml.call&gt;
&lt;programName&gt;MyProgram&lt;/programName&gt;
&lt;pcmlFileLocation&gt;conf:/pcml/my-pcml-file.pcml&lt;/pcmlFileLocation&gt;
&lt;pcmlInputs xmlns:pcml="pcml"&gt;{//pcml:pcmlInputs}&lt;/pcmlInputs&gt;
&lt;pool.returnPoolName&gt;MyConnectionPool&lt;/pool.returnPoolName&gt;
&lt;/pcml.call&gt; </code></pre> Let's assume that there is an RPG program in an AS400 server that performs an addition when two input values are provided. Following will be the PCML source file that is required for this program. This PCML file needs to be stored as /_system/config/pcml/PcmlNumberAddition.pcml resource in the ESB registry.</p> <pre><code>&lt;pcml version="4.0"&gt;
&lt;program name="Addition" path="/QSYS.LIB/%LIBL%.LIB/ADDITION.PGM"&gt;
&lt;data name="inputValue1" type="int" length="4" usage="input" /&gt;
&lt;data name="inputValue2" type="int" length="4" usage="input" /&gt;
&lt;data name="outputValue" type="int" length="4" usage="output" /&gt;
&lt;/program&gt;
&lt;/pcml&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>&lt;p:add xlmns:p="http://services.samples"&gt;
&lt;p:request&gt;
&lt;p:value1&gt;5&lt;/p:value1&gt;
&lt;p:value2&gt;10&lt;/p:value2&gt;
&lt;/p:request&gt;
&lt;/p:add&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample response</p> <pre><code>&lt;&lt;?xml version="1.0" ?&gt;
&lt;xpcml version="6.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation='xpcml.xsd' &gt;
&lt;program name="Addition" path="/QSYS.LIB/%LIBL%.LIB/ADDITION.PGM"&gt;
&lt;parameterList&gt;
&lt;intParm name="inputValue1" passDirection="in"&gt;5&lt;/intParm&gt;
&lt;intParm name="inputValue2" passDirection="in"&gt;10&lt;/intParm&gt;
&lt;intParm name="outputValue" passDirection="out"&gt;15&lt;intParm&gt;
&lt;/parameterList&gt;
&lt;/program&gt;
&lt;/xpcml&gt;
</code></pre>

returnPool<p>The returnPool operation can be used to return the AS400 instance from the mediation flow back into the connection pool.  Parameter Name Description Required returnPoolName  The name of the pool which the AS400 connection needs to be returned to. Yes. </p> <pre><code>&lt;pcml.returnPool&gt;
&lt;pool.returnPoolName&gt;MyConnectionPool&lt;/pool.returnPoolName&gt;
&lt;/pcml.returnPool&gt;
</code></pre>

Administrator<p>The Administrator connection allows you to manage Azure Service Bus resources such as queues, topics, subscriptions, and rules.</p> <p> Parameter Name Display Name Description Required Default Value connectionName Connection Name A unique name to identify this connection. Yes - connectionString Connection String The connection string for the Azure Service Bus namespace. Obtain this from the Azure portal under Shared Access Policies. Yes - </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.init&gt;
&lt;connectionType&gt;ADMINISTRATOR&lt;/connectionType&gt;
&lt;name&gt;asbAdminConnection&lt;/name&gt;
&lt;connectionString&gt;Endpoint=sb://my-namespace.servicebus.windows.net/;SharedAccessKeyName=RootManageSharedAccessKey;SharedAccessKey=xxxxxxxx&lt;/connectionString&gt;
&lt;/asb.init&gt;
</code></pre>

MessageSender<p>The MessageSender connection allows you to send messages to a specific queue or topic.</p> <p> Parameter Name Display Name Description Required Default Value connectionName Connection Name A unique name to identify this connection. Yes - connectionString Connection String The connection string for the Azure Service Bus namespace. Yes - entityType Entity Type The type of Service Bus entity to send messages to. Possible values: <code>QUEUE</code>, <code>TOPIC</code>. Yes - topicOrQueueName Topic or Queue Name The name of the queue or topic to send messages to. Yes - AMQP Retry Options amqpRetryOptions_maxRetries Max Retries The maximum number of retry attempts. No - amqpRetryOptions_delay Delay The initial delay between retry attempts in seconds. No - amqpRetryOptions_maxDelay Max Delay The maximum delay between retry attempts in seconds. No - amqpRetryOptions_tryTimeout Try Timeout The timeout per retry attempt in seconds. No - amqpRetryOptions_retryMode Retry Mode The retry mode to use. Possible values: <code>EXPONENTIAL</code>, <code>FIXED</code>. No - </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.init&gt;
&lt;connectionType&gt;MESSAGE_SENDER&lt;/connectionType&gt;
&lt;name&gt;asbSenderConnection&lt;/name&gt;
&lt;connectionString&gt;Endpoint=sb://my-namespace.servicebus.windows.net/;SharedAccessKeyName=RootManageSharedAccessKey;SharedAccessKey=xxxxxxxx&lt;/connectionString&gt;
&lt;entityType&gt;QUEUE&lt;/entityType&gt;
&lt;topicOrQueueName&gt;myQueue&lt;/topicOrQueueName&gt;
&lt;/asb.init&gt;
</code></pre>

MessageReceiver<p>The MessageReceiver connection allows you to receive messages from a specific queue or topic subscription.</p> <p> Parameter Name Display Name Description Required Default Value connectionName Connection Name A unique name to identify this connection. Yes - connectionString Connection String The connection string for the Azure Service Bus namespace. Yes - entityConfigDataType Entity Config Type The type of entity to receive messages from. Possible values: <code>TopicSubsConfig</code> (for topic subscriptions), <code>QueueConfig</code> (for queues). Yes - Topic Subscription Configuration (when entityConfigDataType is TopicSubsConfig) entityConfig_topicName Topic Name The name of the topic to receive messages from. Yes (for TopicSubsConfig) - entityConfig_subscriptionName Subscription Name The name of the subscription to receive messages from. Yes (for TopicSubsConfig) - Queue Configuration (when entityConfigDataType is QueueConfig) entityConfig_queueName Queue Name The name of the queue to receive messages from. Yes (for QueueConfig) - Receive Options receiveMode Receive Mode The mode for receiving messages. Possible values:     <ul> <li>PEEK_LOCK: Messages are locked for the receiver but not removed from the queue. The receiver must complete, abandon, defer, or dead-letter the message.</li> <li>RECEIVE_AND_DELETE: Messages are immediately removed from the queue upon receipt.</li> </ul> No PEEK_LOCK maxAutoLockRenewDuration Max Auto Lock Renew Duration The maximum duration (in seconds) for automatically renewing message locks. No - AMQP Retry Options amqpRetryOptions_maxRetries Max Retries The maximum number of retry attempts. No - amqpRetryOptions_delay Delay The initial delay between retry attempts in seconds. No - amqpRetryOptions_maxDelay Max Delay The maximum delay between retry attempts in seconds. No - amqpRetryOptions_tryTimeout Try Timeout The timeout per retry attempt in seconds. No - amqpRetryOptions_retryMode Retry Mode The retry mode to use. Possible values: <code>EXPONENTIAL</code>, <code>FIXED</code>. No - </p> <p>Sample configuration (Queue)</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.init&gt;
&lt;connectionType&gt;MESSAGE_RECEIVER&lt;/connectionType&gt;
&lt;name&gt;asbReceiverConnection&lt;/name&gt;
&lt;connectionString&gt;Endpoint=sb://my-namespace.servicebus.windows.net/;SharedAccessKeyName=RootManageSharedAccessKey;SharedAccessKey=xxxxxxxx&lt;/connectionString&gt;
&lt;entityConfigDataType&gt;QueueConfig&lt;/entityConfigDataType&gt;
&lt;entityConfig_queueName&gt;myQueue&lt;/entityConfig_queueName&gt;
&lt;receiveMode&gt;PEEK_LOCK&lt;/receiveMode&gt;
&lt;/asb.init&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample configuration (Topic Subscription)</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.init&gt;
&lt;connectionType&gt;MESSAGE_RECEIVER&lt;/connectionType&gt;
&lt;name&gt;asbReceiverConnection&lt;/name&gt;
&lt;connectionString&gt;Endpoint=sb://my-namespace.servicebus.windows.net/;SharedAccessKeyName=RootManageSharedAccessKey;SharedAccessKey=xxxxxxxx&lt;/connectionString&gt;
&lt;entityConfigDataType&gt;TopicSubsConfig&lt;/entityConfigDataType&gt;
&lt;entityConfig_topicName&gt;myTopic&lt;/entityConfig_topicName&gt;
&lt;entityConfig_subscriptionName&gt;mySubscription&lt;/entityConfig_subscriptionName&gt;
&lt;receiveMode&gt;PEEK_LOCK&lt;/receiveMode&gt;
&lt;/asb.init&gt;
</code></pre>

createQueue<p>Creates a new queue in the Azure Service Bus namespace.</p> <p> Parameter Name Display Name Description Required Default Value queueName Queue Name The name of the queue to create. Yes - Queue Options autoDeleteOnIdle_seconds Auto Delete On Idle (Seconds) The idle interval after which the queue is automatically deleted (seconds component). No - autoDeleteOnIdle_nanoseconds Auto Delete On Idle (Nanoseconds) The idle interval after which the queue is automatically deleted (nanoseconds component). No - defaultMessageTimeToLive_seconds Default Message TTL (Seconds) The default time-to-live for messages in the queue (seconds component). No - defaultMessageTimeToLive_nanoseconds Default Message TTL (Nanoseconds) The default time-to-live for messages in the queue (nanoseconds component). No - duplicateDetectionHistoryTimeWindow_seconds Duplicate Detection Window (Seconds) The duration of the duplicate detection history (seconds component). No - duplicateDetectionHistoryTimeWindow_nanoseconds Duplicate Detection Window (Nanoseconds) The duration of the duplicate detection history (nanoseconds component). No - lockDuration_seconds Lock Duration (Seconds) The lock duration for messages received from the queue (seconds component). No - lockDuration_nanoseconds Lock Duration (Nanoseconds) The lock duration for messages received from the queue (nanoseconds component). No - maxDeliveryCount Max Delivery Count The maximum number of delivery attempts before a message is dead-lettered. No - maxMessageSizeInKilobytes Max Message Size (KB) The maximum message size in kilobytes. No - maxSizeInMegabytes Max Size (MB) The maximum size of the queue in megabytes. No - status Status The status of the queue. Possible values: <code>Active</code>, <code>Disabled</code>, <code>SendDisabled</code>, <code>ReceiveDisabled</code>, <code>Creating</code>, <code>Deleting</code>, <code>Renaming</code>, <code>Restoring</code>, <code>Unknown</code>. No - userMetadata User Metadata Custom metadata associated with the queue. No - enableBatchedOperations Enable Batched Operations Whether to enable batched operations on the queue. No - deadLetteringOnMessageExpiration Dead Lettering On Message Expiration Whether to move expired messages to the dead-letter sub-queue. No - requiresDuplicateDetection Requires Duplicate Detection Whether the queue requires duplicate detection. No - enablePartitioning Enable Partitioning Whether to partition the queue across multiple message brokers. No - requiresSession Requires Session Whether the queue requires sessions for message processing. No - forwardTo Forward To The name of the queue or topic to forward messages to. No - forwardDeadLetteredMessagesTo Forward Dead Lettered Messages To The name of the queue or topic to forward dead-lettered messages to. No - Output responseVariable Response Variable The name of the variable to store the operation output. No - overwriteBody Overwrite Message Body Whether to replace the message body with the operation output. No false </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.createQueue configKey="asbAdminConnection"&gt;
&lt;queueName&gt;myQueue&lt;/queueName&gt;
&lt;maxDeliveryCount&gt;10&lt;/maxDeliveryCount&gt;
&lt;defaultMessageTimeToLive_seconds&gt;3600&lt;/defaultMessageTimeToLive_seconds&gt;
&lt;enableBatchedOperations&gt;true&lt;/enableBatchedOperations&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;asb_createQueue_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;false&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/asb.createQueue&gt;
</code></pre> getQueue<p>Retrieves the properties of a queue.</p> <p> Parameter Name Display Name Description Required Default Value queueName Queue Name The name of the queue to retrieve. Yes - Output responseVariable Response Variable The name of the variable to store the operation output. No - overwriteBody Overwrite Message Body Whether to replace the message body with the operation output. No false </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.getQueue configKey="asbAdminConnection"&gt;
&lt;queueName&gt;myQueue&lt;/queueName&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;asb_getQueue_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;false&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/asb.getQueue&gt;
</code></pre> updateQueue<p>Updates the properties of an existing queue.</p> <p> Parameter Name Display Name Description Required Default Value queueName Queue Name The name of the queue to update. Yes - Update Options autoDeleteOnIdle_seconds Auto Delete On Idle (Seconds) The idle interval after which the queue is automatically deleted (seconds component). No - autoDeleteOnIdle_nanoseconds Auto Delete On Idle (Nanoseconds) The idle interval after which the queue is automatically deleted (nanoseconds component). No - defaultMessageTimeToLive_seconds Default Message TTL (Seconds) The default time-to-live for messages (seconds component). No - defaultMessageTimeToLive_nanoseconds Default Message TTL (Nanoseconds) The default time-to-live for messages (nanoseconds component). No - duplicateDetectionHistoryTimeWindow_seconds Duplicate Detection Window (Seconds) The duration of the duplicate detection history (seconds component). No - duplicateDetectionHistoryTimeWindow_nanoseconds Duplicate Detection Window (Nanoseconds) The duration of the duplicate detection history (nanoseconds component). No - lockDuration_seconds Lock Duration (Seconds) The lock duration for messages (seconds component). No - lockDuration_nanoseconds Lock Duration (Nanoseconds) The lock duration for messages (nanoseconds component). No - maxDeliveryCount Max Delivery Count The maximum number of delivery attempts before a message is dead-lettered. No - maxMessageSizeInKilobytes Max Message Size (KB) The maximum message size in kilobytes. No - maxSizeInMegabytes Max Size (MB) The maximum size of the queue in megabytes. No - status Status The status of the queue. Possible values: <code>Active</code>, <code>Disabled</code>, <code>SendDisabled</code>, <code>ReceiveDisabled</code>, <code>Creating</code>, <code>Deleting</code>, <code>Renaming</code>, <code>Restoring</code>, <code>Unknown</code>. No - userMetadata User Metadata Custom metadata associated with the queue. No - enableBatchedOperations Enable Batched Operations Whether to enable batched operations on the queue. No - deadLetteringOnMessageExpiration Dead Lettering On Message Expiration Whether to move expired messages to the dead-letter sub-queue. No - requiresDuplicateDetection Requires Duplicate Detection Whether the queue requires duplicate detection. No - enablePartitioning Enable Partitioning Whether to partition the queue across multiple message brokers. No - requiresSession Requires Session Whether the queue requires sessions for message processing. No - forwardTo Forward To The name of the queue or topic to forward messages to. No - forwardDeadLetteredMessagesTo Forward Dead Lettered Messages To The name of the queue or topic to forward dead-lettered messages to. No - Output responseVariable Response Variable The name of the variable to store the operation output. No - overwriteBody Overwrite Message Body Whether to replace the message body with the operation output. No false </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.updateQueue configKey="asbAdminConnection"&gt;
&lt;queueName&gt;myQueue&lt;/queueName&gt;
&lt;maxDeliveryCount&gt;15&lt;/maxDeliveryCount&gt;
&lt;status&gt;Active&lt;/status&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;asb_updateQueue_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;false&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/asb.updateQueue&gt;
</code></pre> deleteQueue<p>Deletes a queue from the Azure Service Bus namespace.</p> <p> Parameter Name Display Name Description Required Default Value queueName Queue Name The name of the queue to delete. Yes - Output responseVariable Response Variable The name of the variable to store the operation output. No - overwriteBody Overwrite Message Body Whether to replace the message body with the operation output. No false </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.deleteQueue configKey="asbAdminConnection"&gt;
&lt;queueName&gt;myQueue&lt;/queueName&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;asb_deleteQueue_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;false&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/asb.deleteQueue&gt;
</code></pre> listQueues<p>Lists all queues in the Azure Service Bus namespace.</p> <p> Parameter Name Display Name Description Required Default Value Output responseVariable Response Variable The name of the variable to store the operation output. No - overwriteBody Overwrite Message Body Whether to replace the message body with the operation output. No false </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.listQueues configKey="asbAdminConnection"&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;asb_listQueues_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;false&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;/asb.listQueues&gt;
</code></pre> queueExists<p>Checks whether a queue exists in the Azure Service Bus namespace.</p> <p> Parameter Name Display Name Description Required Default Value queueName Queue Name The name of the queue to check. Yes - Output responseVariable Response Variable The name of the variable to store the operation output. No - overwriteBody Overwrite Message Body Whether to replace the message body with the operation output. No false </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;asb.queueExists configKey="asbAdminConnection"&gt;
&lt;queueName&gt;myQueue&lt;/queueName&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;asb_queueExists_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;false&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
