processDocuments<p>The <code>processDocuments</code> operation submits a document to the configured backend service for data extraction based on a defined schema.  Parameter Name Element Type Description Default Value Required Connection configKey String The LLM connection to use for document processing. - Yes Content Format contentFormat String              The format of the input file content. Allowed values: <code>Base64</code>, <code>Data URI</code>. Note: In MI server, multipart form data will be available as Base64. If you are sending an image as form data, use <code>Base64</code>.          Base64 No MIME Type mimeType String              The MIME type of the file being processed. Allowed values (when using Base64): <code>image/png</code>, <code>image/jpeg</code>, <code>image/gif</code>, <code>image/webp</code>, <code>application/pdf</code> - No Content fileContent String              The content of the image or PDF to be processed, based on the selected content format.          - Yes Schema idpSchema String              The predefined schema for data extraction.             If you do not have a schema, click +Add new schema. Refer to the Schema Generation Reference for more information.          - Yes Max Tokens maxTokens Integer The maximum number of tokens to generate in the completion. 4096 No Response Variable responseVariable String Name of the variable to which the output of the operation should be assigned. - No Overwrite Body overwriteBody Boolean Replace the Message Body in the Message Context with the response of the operation. false No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;idp.processDocuments configKey="ollama_connection_1"&gt;
&lt;maxTokens&gt;4096&lt;/maxTokens&gt;
&lt;fileContent&gt;{${payload.file}}&lt;/fileContent&gt;
&lt;idpSchema&gt;schema_2&lt;/idpSchema&gt;
&lt;responseVariable&gt;idp_processDocuments_1&lt;/responseVariable&gt;
&lt;overwriteBody&gt;true&lt;/overwriteBody&gt;
&lt;contentFormat&gt;Base64&lt;/contentFormat&gt;
&lt;mimeType&gt;image/jpeg&lt;/mimeType&gt;
&lt;/idp.processDocuments&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <p>Following is a sample REST/JSON request that can be handled by the processDocuments operation.</p> <pre><code>{
"file": "&lt;Base64 string&gt;"
}
</code></pre> <p>Response</p> <p>The response may vary based on the defined schema.</p>

getDashboards<p>This operation returns a JSON representation of the list of dashboards, including their names, IDs, and more.  Parameter Name Description Required maxResults The maximum number of dashboards to return, up to 1000 (default is 50). No startAt The index of the first dashboard to return (0-based). Must be 0 or a multiple of maxResults. No filter An optional filter that is applied to the list of dashboards. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;jira.getDashboards&gt;
