"32x32": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&amp;ownerId=fred",
"48x48": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=large&amp;ownerId=fred"
},
"displayName": "Fred F. User",
"active": true,
"timeZone": "Australia/Sydney",
"groups": {
"size": 3,
"items": []
}
}
</code></pre> getUserPermissions<p>To get information on the current user's permissions, use <code>getUserPermissions</code>. You can optionally provide a specific context for which you want to get permissions (projectKey, projectId, issueKey, or issueId).</p> <p> Parameter Name Description Required projectKey/projectId Identifies the project for which you want to determine the current user's permissions. No issueKey/issueId Identifies the issue for which you want to determine the current user's permissions. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;jira.getUserPermissions&gt;
&lt;projectKey&gt;{$ctx:projectKey}&lt;/projectKey&gt;
&lt;projectId&gt;{$ctx:projectId}&lt;/projectId&gt;
&lt;issueKey&gt;{$ctx:issueKey}&lt;/issueKey&gt;
&lt;issueId&gt;{$ctx:issueId}&lt;/issueId&gt;
&lt;/jira.getUserPermissions&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <p>The following is a sample REST/JSON request that can be handled by the <code>getUserPermissions</code> operation.</p> <pre><code>{
"projectKey":"TEST"
}
</code></pre> <p>Sample response</p> <p>Given below is a sample response for the <code>getUserPermissions</code> operation.</p> <pre><code>{
"permissions": {
"EDIT_ISSUE": {
"id": "12",
"key": "EDIT_ISSUE",
"name": "Edit Issues",
"description": "Ability to edit issues.",
"havePermission": true
}
}
}
</code></pre> searchUser<p>To search for users whose username, name, or email address match a search string, use <code>searchUser</code> with a search string.</p> <p> Parameter Name Description Required usernameForSearch The search string used to search the username, name, or email address. Yes startAt The 0-based index of the first user to return (default is 0). No maxResults The maximum number of users to return, up to 1000 (default is 50). No includeActive Whether to return active users (default is true). No includeInactive Whether to return inactive users (default is false). No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;jira.searchUser&gt;
&lt;usernameForSearch&gt;{$ctx:usernameForSearch}&lt;/usernameForSearch&gt;
&lt;startAt&gt;{$ctx:startAt}&lt;/startAt&gt;
&lt;maxResults&gt;{$ctx:maxResults}&lt;/maxResults&gt;
&lt;includeActive&gt;{$ctx:includeActive}&lt;/includeActive&gt;
&lt;includeInactive&gt;{$ctx:includeInactive}&lt;/includeInactive&gt;
&lt;/jira.searchUser&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <p>The following is a sample REST/JSON request that can be handled by the <code>searchUser</code> operation.</p> <pre><code>{
"usernameForSearch":"fred"
}
</code></pre> <p>Sample response</p> <p>Given below is a sample response for the <code>searchUser</code> operation.</p> <pre><code>[
{
"self": "http://localhost:8080/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=fred",
"name": "fred",
"avatarUrls": {
"24x24": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&amp;ownerId=fred",
"16x16": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&amp;ownerId=fred",
"32x32": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&amp;ownerId=fred",
"48x48": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=large&amp;ownerId=fred"
},
"displayName": "Fred F. User",
"active": false
}
]
</code></pre> searchIssueViewableUsers<p>To search for users whose username, name, or email address match a search string and have permission to view the specified issue or project, use <code>searchIssueViewableUsers</code>. You need to specify the search string and issue key or project key.</p> <p> Parameter Name Description Required username The search string used to search the username, name, or email address. Yes projectKey If you want to search for users who can browse a project instead of a specific issue, specify projectKey instead of issueKey. Yes issueKey Identifies the issue that users must have permission to view. This issue will be included in the results. No startAt The 0-based index of the first user to return (default is 0). No maxResults The maximum number of users to return, up to 1000 (default is 50). No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;jira.searchIssueViewableUsers&gt;
&lt;usernameForSearch&gt;{$ctx:usernameForSearch}&lt;/usernameForSearch&gt;
&lt;issueKey&gt;{$ctx:issueKey}&lt;/issueKey&gt;
&lt;projectKey&gt;{$ctx:projectKey}&lt;/projectKey&gt;
&lt;startAt&gt;{$ctx:startAt}&lt;/startAt&gt;
&lt;maxResults&gt;{$ctx:maxResults}&lt;/maxResults&gt;
&lt;/jira.searchIssueViewableUsers&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <p>The following is a sample REST/JSON request that can be handled by the searchIssueViewableUsers operation.</p> <pre><code>{
"usernameForSearch":"fred",
"projectKey":"TEST"
}
</code></pre> <p>Sample response</p> <p>Given below is a sample response for the <code>searchIssueViewableUsers</code> operation.</p> <pre><code>[
{
"self": "http://localhost:8080/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=fred",
"name": "fred",
"avatarUrls": {
"24x24": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&amp;ownerId=fred",
"16x16": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&amp;ownerId=fred",
"32x32": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&amp;ownerId=fred",
"48x48": "http://localhost:8080/jira/secure/useravatar?size=large&amp;ownerId=fred"
},
"displayName": "Fred F. User",
"active": false
}
]
</code></pre> searchAssignableUser<p>To search for users whose username, name, or email address match a search string and can be assigned to a specific issue, use <code>searchAssignableUser</code>. You specify the search string and either the project key (if you are getting users for a new issue you are creating) or the issue key (if you are getting users for an existing issue you are editing).</p> <p> Parameter Name Description Required project Identifies the project in which you are creating a new issue and want to get a list of users who can be assigned to it. Yes usernameForSearch The search string used to search the username, name, or email address. Yes issueKey Identifies the issue that users must have permission to view. This issue will be included in the results. No issueKey Identifies the issue you are editing so that you can get a list of users who can be assigned to it. No startAt The 0-based index of the first user to return (default is 0). No maxResults The maximum number of users to return, up to 1000 (default is 50). No actionDescriptorId The id of the workflow action. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;jira.searchAssignableUser&gt;
&lt;usernameForSearch&gt;{$ctx:usernameForSearch}&lt;/usernameForSearch&gt;
&lt;project&gt;{$ctx:project}&lt;/project&gt;
&lt;issueKey&gt;{$ctx:issueKey}&lt;/issueKey&gt;
&lt;startAt&gt;{$ctx:startAt}&lt;/startAt&gt;
&lt;maxResults&gt;{$ctx:maxResults}&lt;/maxResults&gt;
&lt;actionDescriptorId&gt;{$ctx:actionDescriptorId}&lt;/actionDescriptorId&gt;
&lt;/jira.searchAssignableUser&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <p>The following is a sample REST/JSON request that can be handled by the <code>searchAssignableUser</code> operation.</p> <pre><code>{
"projectKey":"TEST"
}
</code></pre> <p>Sample response</p> <p>Given below is a sample response for the <code>searchAssignableUser</code> operation.</p> <pre><code>{
"self": "http://localhost:8080/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=fred",
"name": "fred",
