</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"sObjectName":"Account",
"rowId":"00128000005YjDnAAK",
}
</code></pre>

compositeBatch<p>The <code>salesforce.compositeBatch</code> operation executes up to 25 sub-requests in a single call to Salesforce’s Composite Batch REST resource. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value Field and Value JSON string that defines the array of sub-requests (each sub-request includes <code>method</code>, <code>url</code>, optional <code>body</code>, and a <code>referenceId</code>). Yes [{"method":"GET","url":"/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account/001..."}] </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforce.compositeBatch&gt;
&lt;fieldAndValue&gt;{${payload.fieldAndValue}}&lt;/fieldAndValue&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.compositeBatch&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"fieldAndValue": {
"batchRequests": [
{
"method": "PATCH",
"url": "v64.0/sobjects/account/001D000000K0fXOIAZ",
"richInput": {
"Name": "NewName"
}
},
{
"method": "GET",
"url": "v64.0/sobjects/account/001D000000K0fXOIAZ?fields=Name,BillingPostalCode"
}
]
}
}
</code></pre> compositeGraph<p>The <code>salesforce.compositeGraph</code> operation submits one or more composite graph operations to Salesforce’s Composite Graph REST resource. Each graph can contain multiple sub-requests that are executed in the order you define. See the Composite Graph API documentation for full details.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value Field and Value              A JSON object that defines one or more graphs.             Each graph contains a <code>graphId</code> and a <code>compositeRequest</code> array.             Every sub-request in <code>compositeRequest</code> specifies <code>method</code>, <code>url</code>, an optional <code>body</code>, and a <code>referenceId</code>.          Yes { "graphs": [ { "graphId": "Graph1", "compositeRequest": [ … ] } ] } </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforce.compositeGraph&gt;
&lt;fieldAndValue&gt;{${payload.fieldAndValue}}&lt;/fieldAndValue&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.compositeGraph&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"fieldAndValue": {
"graphs": [
{
"graphId": "Graph1",
"compositeRequest": [
{
"method": "GET",
"url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account/0018g00000XXXXXAAA",
"referenceId": "RefAccount"
},
{
"method": "PATCH",
"url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account/@{RefAccount.Id}",
"body": {
"Industry": "Manufacturing"
},
"referenceId": "UpdateAccount"
}
]
}
]
}
}
</code></pre> compositeRequest<p>The <code>salesforce.compositeRequest</code> operation executes a series of REST API sub-requests in a single call to Salesforce’s Composite REST resource, preserving the order and allowing inter-request references. See the Composite API documentation for full details.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value Field And Value              A JSON object that defines the composite request.             Must include an <code>allOrNone</code> flag and a <code>compositeRequest</code> array.             Each item in <code>compositeRequest</code> specifies <code>method</code>, <code>url</code>, an optional <code>body</code>, and a <code>referenceId</code>.          Yes { "allOrNone": true, "compositeRequest": [ … ] } </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforce.compositeRequest&gt;
&lt;fieldAndValue&gt;{${payload.fieldAndValue}}&lt;/fieldAndValue&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.compositeRequest&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"fieldAndValue": {
"allOrNone": true,
"compositeRequest": [
{
"method": "GET",
"url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account/0018g00000XXXXXAAA",
"referenceId": "RefAccount"
},
{
"method": "PATCH",
"url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account/@{RefAccount.id}",
"body": {
"Industry": "Manufacturing"
},
"referenceId": "UpdateAccount"
},
{
"method": "POST",
"url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Contact",
"body": {
"LastName": "Smith",
"AccountId": "@{RefAccount.id}"
},
"referenceId": "CreateContact"
}
]
}
}
</code></pre>

abortJob<p>The <code>salesforce.abortJob</code> operation aborts a bulk ingest job in Salesforce using Salesforce Bulk API v2. See the related API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value Salesforce configuration The Salesforce configuration that stores OAuth-related data. Yes salesforceConfig Job ID The bulk job ID. Yes 7503i000000XXXXXAAI </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforce.abortJob&gt;
&lt;jobId&gt;{${payload.jobId}}&lt;/jobId&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.abortJob&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
