"batchSize": 200,
"queryString": "SELECT Id, Name FROM Account"
}
</code></pre> soapQueryAll<p>The <code>salesforce.soapQueryAll</code> operation runs a SOQL query that returns both active and archived/deleted records. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value Batch Size The number of records to return. Yes 200 Query String The queryString to get the results from API. Yes SELECT Id, Name FROM Account </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforce.soapQueryAll&gt;
&lt;batchSize&gt;{${payload.batchSize}}&lt;/batchSize&gt;
&lt;queryString&gt;{${payload.queryString}}&lt;/queryString&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapQueryAll&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"batchSize": 200,
"queryString": "SELECT Id, Name FROM Account"
}
</code></pre> soapQueryMore<p>The <code>salesforce.soapQueryMore</code> operation retrieves the next batch of query results. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value Batch Size The number of records to return. Yes 200 </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforce.soapQueryMore&gt;
&lt;batchSize&gt;{${payload.batchSize}}&lt;/batchSize&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapQueryMore&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"batchSize": 200
}
</code></pre> soapResetPassword<p>The <code>salesforce.soapResetPassword</code> operation resets a user's password and emails them the new password. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value User ID The user's Salesforce ID. Yes 0058g00000XXXXXAAA </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforce.soapResetPassword&gt;
&lt;userId&gt;{${payload.userId}}&lt;/userId&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapResetPassword&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"userId": "0058g00000XXXXXAAA"
}
</code></pre> soapRetrieve<p>The <code>salesforce.soapRetrieve</code> operation retrieves field values for one or more records of a specified object. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value Object Type The object type of the records. Yes Account Object IDs XML representation of the records to retrieve, as shown in the following example. Yes &lt;ids&gt;001...&lt;/ids&gt; Field List A comma-separated list of the fields you want to retrieve from the records. Yes SampleValue </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforce.soapRetrieve&gt;
&lt;objectType&gt;{${payload.objectType}}&lt;/objectType&gt;
&lt;objectIDS&gt;{${payload.objectIDS}}&lt;/objectIDS&gt;
&lt;fieldList&gt;{${payload.fieldList}}&lt;/fieldList&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapRetrieve&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"objectType": "Account",
"objectIDS": "&lt;ids&gt;001...&lt;/ids&gt;",
"fieldList": "SampleValue"
}
</code></pre> soapSearch<p>The <code>salesforce.soapSearch</code> operation executes a SOSL text search against your organization's data. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value search String The searchString to get the Result. Yes John </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforce.soapSearch&gt;
&lt;searchString&gt;{${payload.searchString}}&lt;/searchString&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapSearch&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"searchString": "*John*"
}
</code></pre> soapSendEmail<p>The <code>salesforce.soapSendEmail</code> operation sends a single or mass email immediately. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value Send Email XML representation of the email, as shown in the example. Yes {} </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>    &lt;salesforce.soapSendEmail&gt;
&lt;sendEmail&gt;{${payload.sendEmail}}&lt;/sendEmail&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapSendEmail&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>    {
"sendEmail": "&lt;SingleEmailMessage&gt;...&lt;/SingleEmailMessage&gt;"
}
</code></pre> soapSendEmailMessage<p>The <code>salesforce.soapSendEmailMessage</code> operation sends up to 10 draft EmailMessage records. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value Send Email Message XML representation of the email IDs to send, as shown in the example. Yes {} </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>    &lt;salesforce.soapSendEmailMessage&gt;
&lt;sendEmailMessage&gt;{${payload.sendEmailMessage}}&lt;/sendEmailMessage&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapSendEmailMessage&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>    {
"sendEmailMessage": "&lt;EmailMessage&gt;...&lt;/EmailMessage&gt;"
}
</code></pre> soapSetPassword<p>The <code>salesforce.soapSetPassword</code> operation sets a user's password to a specified value. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value User ID The user's Salesforce ID. Yes 0058g00000XXXXXAAA Password If using setPassword, the new password to assign to the user. Yes P@ssw0rd123 </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>    &lt;salesforce.soapSetPassword&gt;
&lt;userId&gt;{${payload.userId}}&lt;/userId&gt;
&lt;password&gt;{${payload.password}}&lt;/password&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapSetPassword&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>    {
"userId": "0058g00000XXXXXAAA",
"password": "P@ssw0rd123"
}
</code></pre> soapUndelete<p>The <code>salesforce.soapUndelete</code> operation restores deleted records from the Recycle Bin. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value All or None Whether to rollback changes if an object fails(Default value is 0). Yes 1 sObjects The sobject type Yes Account </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>    &lt;salesforce.soapUndelete&gt;
&lt;allOrNone&gt;{${payload.allOrNone}}&lt;/allOrNone&gt;
&lt;sobjects&gt;{${payload.sobjects}}&lt;/sobjects&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapUndelete&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>    {
"allOrNone": "1",
"sobjects": "Account"
}
</code></pre> soapUpdate<p>The <code>salesforce.soapUpdate</code> operation updates one or more existing records. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value All or None Whether to rollback changes if an object fails(Default value is 0). Yes 1 Allow Field Truncate Whether to truncates strings that exceed the field length(Default value is 0). Yes 1 sObjects The sobject type Yes Account </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>    &lt;salesforce.soapUpdate&gt;
&lt;allOrNone&gt;{${payload.allOrNone}}&lt;/allOrNone&gt;
&lt;allowFieldTruncate&gt;{${payload.allowFieldTruncate}}&lt;/allowFieldTruncate&gt;
&lt;sobjects&gt;{${payload.sobjects}}&lt;/sobjects&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapUpdate&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>    {
"allOrNone": "1",
"allowFieldTruncate": "1",
"sobjects": "Account"
}
</code></pre> soapUpsert<p>The <code>salesforce.soapUpsert</code> operation creates new records or updates existing records based on an external ID field. See the SOAP API documentation for more information.  Parameter Name Description Required Sample Value All or None Whether to rollback changes if an object fails(Default value is 0). Yes 1 Allow Field Truncate Whether to truncates strings that exceed the field length(Default value is 0). Yes 1 sObjects The sobject type Yes Account External ID The field containing the record ID Yes External_Id__c </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>    &lt;salesforce.soapUpsert&gt;
&lt;allOrNone&gt;{${payload.allOrNone}}&lt;/allOrNone&gt;
&lt;allowFieldTruncate&gt;{${payload.allowFieldTruncate}}&lt;/allowFieldTruncate&gt;
&lt;sobjects&gt;{${payload.sobjects}}&lt;/sobjects&gt;
&lt;externalId&gt;{${payload.externalId}}&lt;/externalId&gt;
&lt;/salesforce.soapUpsert&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>    {
"allOrNone": "1",
"allowFieldTruncate": "1",
"sobjects": "Account",
"externalId": "External_Id__c"
}
</code></pre>

createAsset<p>The <code>createAsset</code> operation creates a new asset.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>payload</code> The properties required to create a new asset. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>customerKey</code> Reference to customer's private ID/name for the asset. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>contentType</code> The type that the content attribute will be in. No <code>data</code> Property bag containing the asset data. No <code>assetType</code> The type of the asset saved as a name/ID pair. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>version</code> The version of the asset. No <code>locked</code> Specifies if the asset can be modified or not. No <code>fileProperties</code> Properties referred to by the asset if it is a file type. No <code>name</code> Name of the asset, set by the client. 200 character maximum. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>description</code> Description of the asset, set by the client. No <code>category</code> ID of the category the asset belongs to. No <code>tags</code> List of tags associated with the asset. No <code>content</code> The actual content of the asset. No <code>design</code> Fallback for display when neither content nor supercontent are provided. No <code>superContent</code> Content that supersedes content in terms of display. No <code>customFields</code> Custom fields within an asset. No <code>views</code> Views within an asset. No <code>blocks</code> Blocks within the asset. No <code>minBlocks</code> Minimum number of blocks within an asset. No <code>maxBlocks</code> Maximum number of blocks within an asset. No <code>channels</code> List of channels that are allowed to use this asset. No <code>allowedBlocks</code> List of blocks that are allowed in the asset. No <code>slots</code> Slots within the asset. No <code>businessUnitAvailability</code> A dictionary of member IDs that have been granted access to the asset. No <code>template</code> Template the asset follows. No <code>file</code> Base64-encoded string of a file associated with an asset. No <code>generateFrom</code> Indicates which view to use to generate this view’s content. No <code>sharingProperties</code> Allows you to share content with business units with Content Builder Sharing enabled. No <code>sharingProperties.sharedWith</code> List of MID IDs the asset is shared with. No <code>sharingProperties.sharingType</code> Permission granted to MIDs in <code>sharedWith</code> (view, edit, or local). No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.createAsset configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.createAsset&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"body": {
"assetType": {
"name": "htmlemail",
"id": 208
},
"name": "Example Email Created via API",
"customerKey": "MyUniqueEmailAssetKey",
"views": {
"html": {
"content": "&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hello, this is an email from the SFMC API!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"
}
}
}
}
</code></pre> Create Campaign<p>The <code>Create Campaign</code> operation creates a new marketing campaign with defined objectives, target audience, and parameters.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>payload</code> The properties required to create a new campaign. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>name</code> The name of the campaign. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>description</code> A description of the campaign. No <code>campaignCode</code> A campaign code to associate with the campaign. No <code>color</code> The color used to identify the campaign in the Marketing Cloud Engagement web interface, expressed as an HTML color code. No <code>favorite</code> Indicates whether to identify the campaign as a favorite. No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;SalesforceMarketingCloud.createCampaign configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/SalesforceMarketingCloud.createCampaign&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"body": {
"name": "Final Hours for Summer Sale",
"description": "Invite our most engaged customers to shop our Summer Sale before it ends.",
"campaignCode": "summer2023",
"color": "800080",
"favorite": false
}
}
</code></pre> createCategory<p>The <code>createCategory</code> operation creates a category (folder) in content builder.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>payload</code> The properties required to create a new category. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>name</code> Name of the category. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>parentId</code> ID of the parent category. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>categoryType</code> The type of category, either asset or asset-shared, automatically set to match the parent. If asset-shared, include SharingProperties. No <code>enterpriseId</code> ID of the enterprise this business unit belongs to. No <code>memberId</code> ID of the member who creates the category. No <code>description</code> Description of the category. No <code>sharingProperties</code> Allows sharing the category with business units with Content Builder Sharing enabled. Includes MIDs and sharing type. No <code>sharingProperties.sharedWith</code> List of up to 100 MID IDs the category is shared with. Use 0 to share across the enterprise if enabled. No <code>sharingProperties.sharingType</code> Permission for MIDs in <code>sharedWith</code>. Only possible value for categories is <code>edit</code>. No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.createCategory configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.createCategory&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"body": {
"name": "My New Folder",
"parentId": 50923,
"enterpriseId": 123456,
"categoryType": "asset"
}
}
</code></pre> createContact<p>The <code>createContact</code> operation creates a new contact with the specified information in the specified attribute groups.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>payload</code> The properties required to create a new contact. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>contactKey</code> Primary address for the contact. You must provide either a value for contactKey or contactID. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>contactID</code> Unique ID for the contact. You must provide either a value for contactKey or contactID. No <code>attributeSets</code> Array of information used to create a new contact. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>attributeSets.name</code> Required. Name of attribute group to which to add the contact information. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>attributeSets.values</code> Name and value pairs indicating the attribute and applicable value. No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.createContact configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.createContact&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"body": {
"contactKey": "acruz@mycompany.com",
"attributeSets": [
{
"name": "Email Addresses",
"items": [
{
"values": [
{
"name": "Email Address",
"value": "acruz@mycompany.com"
},
{
"name": "HTML Enabled",
"value": true
}
]
}
]
}
]
}
}
</code></pre> createJourney<p>The <code>createJourney</code> operation creates or saves a journey.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>payload</code> The properties required to create a new journey. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>key</code> Required. The customer key as a GUID (UUID) to be used while referencing this journey. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>name</code> Required. The name of this journey. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>description</code> A description of this journey. No <code>workflowApiVersion</code> Required. The Journey Spec version to use for this journey. Possible values: 0.5, 1.0. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>goals</code> The goal for this particular journey. Expressed as an object of type ContactDecision from the Journey Spec. No <code>triggers</code> The trigger for this particular journey. Expressed as an object of type ContactEvent from the Journey Spec. No <code>activities</code> The activities which compose this particular journey. Expressed as objects of types supported by the Journey Spec. No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.createJourney configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.createJourney&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"body": {
"key": "b3102b1f-3fa1-478f-9ca9-665b551e13e6",
"name": "My Journey",
"workflowApiVersion": 1.0,
"description": "A journey created via the API",
"goals": [],
"triggers": [],
"activities": []
}
}
</code></pre> createEmailDefinition<p>The <code>createEmailDefinition</code> operation creates a long-living send definition object that references the email template, subscriber list, sending options, journey, and metadata.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>payload</code> The properties required to create a new email definition. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>definitionKey</code> Required. Unique, user-generated key to access the definition object. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>name</code> Required. Name of the definition. Must be unique. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>content.customerKey</code> Required. Unique identifier of the content asset. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>status</code> Operational state of the definition: active, inactive, or deleted. No <code>description</code> User-provided description of the send definition. No <code>classification</code> The external key of a sending classification defined in Email Studio Administration. Only transactional classifications are permitted. No <code>subscriptions.list</code> Required. The external key of the list or all subscribers. Contains the subscriber keys and profile attributes. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>subscriptions.dataExtension</code> The external key of the triggered send data extension. No <code>subscriptions.autoAddSubscriber</code> Adds the recipient’s email address and contact key as a subscriber key to subscriptions.list. Default is true. No <code>subscriptions.updateSubscriber</code> Updates the recipient’s contact key as a subscriber key. Default is true. No <code>options.trackLinks</code> Wraps links for tracking and reporting. Default is true. No <code>options.cc</code> Include CC email addresses with every send. Can use %%attribute%% syntax for dynamic CCs. No <code>options.bcc</code> Include BCC email addresses with every send. Can use %%attribute%% syntax for dynamic BCCs. No <code>options.createJourney</code> Marks the definition as available for use in Journey Builder as a Transactional Send Journey. No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.createEmailDefinition configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.createEmailDefinition&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"body": {
"definitionKey": "MySendDefinitionKey",
"name": "MySendDefinition",
"content": {
"customerKey": "2ac9d669-59d0-4cf0-aa1f-da6cbf667f1f"
},
"status": "Active",
"description": "Send definition for marketing emails",
"classification": "default transactional",
"subscriptions": {
"list": "MY_PUBLICATION_LIST_KEY",
"dataExtension": "AB8F0F80-065C-4B1C-85FC-545DB1D55768",
"autoAddSubscriber": true,
"updateSubscriber": true
},
"options": {
"trackLinks": true
}
}
}
</code></pre> createSmsDefinition<p>The <code>createSmsDefinition</code> operation creates an sms send definition.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>payload</code> The properties required to create a new SMS definition. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>definitionKey</code> Required. Unique, user-generated key to access the definition object. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>name</code> Required. Name of the definition. Must be unique. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>content.message</code> Required. The message content that you want sent with each message. Use substitution strings and AMPscript to personalize the message. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>status</code> Operational state of the definition: active, inactive, or deleted. No <code>description</code> User-provided description of the send definition. No <code>subscriptions.shortCode</code> Required. The short or long code for the mobile transmissions for each message on this definition. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>subscriptions.countryCode</code> The country code associated with the shortCode. Don't use for long codes unless required by your account configuration. No <code>subscriptions.keyword</code> Required. The keyword used to track messages. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>subscriptions.autoAddSubscriber</code> Allows you to add a recipient as a subscriber using contactKey. When false, the message is rejected if contactKey doesn't exist as a subscriber. No <code>options.urlShortenerOptions.IsLinkShorteningEnabled</code> Indicates if URL shortening is enabled for URLs in the message body. No <code>options.urlShortenerOptions.isSubscriberTrackingEnabled</code> Indicates if subscriber-level tracking is enabled. Required if shortenerType is <code>SFMC</code>. No <code>options.urlShortenerOptions.shortenerType</code> The type of URL shortener. The value is <code>SFMC</code>. No <code>options.SmsMessageRegulatoryAuthorityTemplateId</code> The ID of the DLT template used in the SMS. Available only for customers in India. No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.createSmsDefinition configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.createSmsDefinition&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"body": {
"definitionKey": "account-reset",
"name": "account-reset",
"description": "Using SMS Transactional API",
"content": {
"message": "%%FirstName%%, your 2FA token is %%password%%"
},
"subscriptions": {
"shortCode": "8201221",
"countryCode": "US",
"keyword": "PASSWORD"
},
"options": {
"urlShortenerOptions": {
"isLinkShorteningEnabled": true,
"isSubscriberTrackingEnabled": true,
"shortenerType": "SFMC"
},
"smsMessageRegulatoryAuthorityTemplateId": "1107170833298425627"
}
}
}
</code></pre> getAssets<p>The <code>getAssets</code> operation retrieves an asset collection by simple filter parameters.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>page</code> Page number to return from the paged results. No <code>pagesize</code> Number of results per page to return. No <code>orderBy</code> Determines which asset property to use for sorting, and also determines the direction in which to sort the data. No <code>filter</code> Filter by an asset's property using a simple operator and value. No <code>fields</code> Comma-delimited string of asset properties used to reduce the size of your results to only the properties you need. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.getAssets configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;page&gt;{${payload.page}}&lt;/page&gt;
&lt;pagesize&gt;{${payload.pagesize}}&lt;/pagesize&gt;
&lt;orderBy&gt;{${payload.orderBy}}&lt;/orderBy&gt;
&lt;filter&gt;{${payload.filter}}&lt;/filter&gt;
&lt;fields&gt;{${payload.fields}}&lt;/fields&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.getAssets&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"page": 1,
"pagesize": 10,
"orderBy": "assetId asc",
"filter": "status eq 'active'",
"fields": "assetId,name,status"
}
</code></pre> getCampaigns<p>The <code>getCampaigns</code> operation retrieve a list of campaigns in your account.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>page</code> Page number to return from the paged results. No <code>pagesize</code> Number of results per page to return. No <code>orderBy</code> The field and sort method to use to sort the results. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;SalesforceMarketingCloud.getCampaigns configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;page&gt;{${payload.page}}&lt;/page&gt;
&lt;pagesize&gt;{${payload.pagesize}}&lt;/pagesize&gt;
&lt;orderBy&gt;{${payload.orderBy}}&lt;/orderBy&gt;
&lt;/SalesforceMarketingCloud.getCampaigns&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <p>```json {     "page": 1,     "pagesize": 10,     "orderBy": "assetId asc",     "filter": "status eq 'active'",     "fields": "assetId,name,status" }</p> getContactDeleteRequests<p>The <code>getContactDeleteRequests</code> operation retrieves details of contact delete requests for a date range.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>startdateutc</code> Start date and time in UTC of the date range. No <code>enddateutc</code> End date and time in UTC of the date range. No <code>statusid</code> Delete request status ID. No <code>page</code> Page number to return from the paged results. No <code>pagesize</code> Number of results per page to return. No <code>orderBy</code> Determines which asset property to use for sorting, and also determines the direction in which to sort the data. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.getContactDeleteRequests configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;startdateutc&gt;{${payload.startdateutc}}&lt;/startdateutc&gt;
&lt;enddateutc&gt;{${payload.enddateutc}}&lt;/enddateutc&gt;
&lt;statusid&gt;{${payload.statusid}}&lt;/statusid&gt;
&lt;page&gt;{${payload.page}}&lt;/page&gt;
&lt;pagesize&gt;{${payload.pagesize}}&lt;/pagesize&gt;
&lt;orderBy&gt;{${payload.orderBy}}&lt;/orderBy&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.getContactDeleteRequests&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"startdateutc": "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z",
"enddateutc": "2021-01-31T23:59:59Z",
"statusid": 1,
"pagesize": 50,
"page": 1,
"orderBy": "status asc"
}
</code></pre> getJourneys<p>The <code>getJourneys</code> operation retrieves a list of journeys.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>page</code> The page number of results to retrieve. No <code>pageSize</code> The number of items to return on a page of results. No <code>orderBy</code> The field and sort method to use to sort the results. You can sort on these fields: ModifiedDate, Name, Performance. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.getJourneys configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;page&gt;{${payload.page}}&lt;/page&gt;
&lt;pageSize&gt;{${payload.pageSize}}&lt;/pageSize&gt;
&lt;orderBy&gt;{${payload.orderBy}}&lt;/orderBy&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.getJourneys&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"orderBy": "modifiedDate DESC",
"page": 1,
"pageSize": 50
}
</code></pre> getCategories<p>The <code>getCategories</code> operation returns one or more content builder categories that are owned by or reside in your mid.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>page</code> Page number to return from the paged results. Start with 1 and continue until you get zero results. Typically provided along with the pagesize parameter. No <code>pagesize</code> Number of results per page to return. Typically provided along with the page parameter. No <code>orderBy</code> Determines which category property to use for sorting, and also determines the direction in which to sort the data. No <code>filter</code> Filter by ParentId using a simple operator and value. ParentId is the only allowed field. If you don't provide a filter parameter, the query returns all the Categories in your MID. No </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.getCategories configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;page&gt;{${payload.page}}&lt;/page&gt;
&lt;pagesize&gt;{${payload.pagesize}}&lt;/pagesize&gt;
&lt;orderBy&gt;{${payload.orderBy}}&lt;/orderBy&gt;
&lt;filter&gt;{${payload.filter}}&lt;/filter&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.getCategories&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"filter": "ParentId eq 1234",
"page": 1,
"pagesize": 50,
"orderBy": "categoryId asc"
}
</code></pre> updateAsset<p>The <code>updateAsset</code> operation updates a full asset.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>assetId</code> The ID of the asset to update. Yes <code>payload</code> The properties required to update the asset. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>customerKey</code> Reference to customer's private ID/name for the asset. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>contentType</code> The type that the content attribute will be in. No <code>data</code> Property bag containing the asset data. No <code>assetType</code> The type of the asset saved as a name/ID pair. No <code>version</code> The version of the asset. No <code>locked</code> Specifies if the asset can be modified or not. No <code>fileProperties</code> Stores the different properties that this asset refers to if it is a file type. No <code>name</code> Name of the asset, set by the client. 200 character maximum. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>description</code> Description of the asset, set by the client. No <code>category</code> ID of the category the asset belongs to. No <code>tags</code> List of tags associated with the asset. No <code>content</code> The actual content of the asset. No <code>design</code> Fallback for display when neither content nor supercontent are provided. No <code>superContent</code> Content that supersedes content in terms of display. No <code>customFields</code> Custom fields within an asset. No <code>views</code> Views within an asset. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>blocks</code> Blocks within the asset. No <code>minBlocks</code> Minimum number of blocks within an asset. No <code>maxBlocks</code> Maximum number of blocks within an asset. No <code>channels</code> List of channels that are allowed to use this asset. No <code>allowedBlocks</code> List of blocks that are allowed in the asset. No <code>slots</code> Slots within the asset. No <code>businessUnitAvailability</code> A dictionary of member IDs that have been granted access to the asset. No <code>template</code> Template the asset follows. No <code>file</code> Base64-encoded string of a file associated with an asset. No <code>generateFrom</code> Tells the sending compiler what view to use for generating this view's content. No <code>sharingProperties</code> Allows you to share content with one or more business units that have Content Builder Sharing enabled. No <code>sharingProperties.sharedWith</code> List of MID IDs the asset is shared with. No <code>sharingProperties.sharingType</code> Indicates the permission that you are granting to the list of MIDs in sharedWith. Possible values are view, edit, or local. No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.updateAsset configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;assetId&gt;{${payload.assetId}}&lt;/assetId&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.updateAsset&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"assetId": 3456,
"body": {
"CustomerKey": "example-key-123",
"ContentType": "text/html",
"Data": {
"htmlContent": "&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Sample Content&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"
},
"AssetType": {
"Name": "html",
"ID": 1
},
"Version": 1,
"Locked": false,
"Name": "Sample Asset",
"Description": "This is a sample asset update",
"Category": {
"ID": 10
},
"Tags": [
"sample",
"asset"
],
"Content": "&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Updated Content&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"
}
}
</code></pre> updateContact<p>The <code>updateContact</code> operation updates a contact record.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>payload</code> The properties required to update the contact. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>contactKey</code> Primary address for the contact. You must provide either a value for contactKey or contactID. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>contactID</code> Unique ID for the contact. You must provide either a value for contactKey or contactID. No <code>attributeSets</code> Array of information used to create a new contact. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>attributeSets.name</code> Required. Name of attribute group to which to add the contact information. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>attributeSets.values</code> Name and value pairs indicating the attribute and applicable value. No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.updateContact configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.updateContact&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"body": {
"contactKey": "john.doe@example.com",
"contactId": 123456,
"attributeSets": [
{
"name": "Email Addresses",
"items": [
{
"values": [
{
"name": "Email Address",
"value": "john.doe@example.com"
},
{
"name": "HTML Enabled",
"value": true
}
]
}
]
}
]
}
}
</code></pre> updateCampaign<p>The <code>updateCampaign</code> operation updates a campaign.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>campaignId</code> ID of the campaign to be updated. Yes <code>payload</code> The properties required to update the campaign. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>INLINE</code> <code>name</code> The name of the campaign. Required if <code>inputStructure</code> is <code>FORM</code> <code>description</code> A description of the campaign. No <code>campaignCode</code> A campaign code to associate with the campaign. No <code>color</code> The color used to identify the campaign in the Marketing Cloud Engagement web interface, expressed as an HTML color code. No <code>favorite</code> Indicates whether to identify the campaign as a favorite. No </p> <p>Sample configuration for "INLINE"</p> <pre><code>&lt;SalesforceMarketingCloud.updateCampaign configKey="OSCON"&gt;
&lt;inputStructure&gt;INLINE&lt;/inputStructure&gt;
&lt;campaignId&gt;{${payload.id}}&lt;/campaignId&gt;
&lt;payload&gt;{${payload.body}}&lt;/payload&gt;
&lt;/SalesforceMarketingCloud.updateCampaign&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <pre><code>{
"id": 237
"body": {
"name": "Final Hours for Summer Sale",
"description": "Invite our most engaged customers to shop our Summer Sale before it ends.",
"campaignCode": "summer2023",
"color": "800080",
"favorite": false
}
}
</code></pre> deleteAsset<p>The <code>deleteAsset</code> operation deletes an asset.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>assetId</code> The ID of the asset to delete. Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.deleteAsset configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;assetId&gt;{${payload.assetId}}&lt;/assetId&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.deleteAsset&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <p>```json {     "assetId": 3456 }</p> deleteCampaign<p>The <code>deleteCampaign</code> operation deletes a campaign.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>campaignId</code> The ID of the campaign to delete. Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;salesforceMarketingCloud.deleteCampaign configKey="SFMC_CON"&gt;
&lt;campaignId&gt;{${payload.campaignId}}&lt;/campaignId&gt;
&lt;/salesforceMarketingCloud.deleteCampaign&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Sample request</p> <p>```json {     "campaignId": 3456 }</p> deleteContact<p>The <code>deleteContact</code> operation deletes a given list of contacts.  Parameter Name Description Required <code>values</code> Array of contact ID values to delete. Yes <code>deleteOperationType</code> Type of delete operation to perform. Yes </p> <p>Sample configuration</p> <pre><code>&lt;SalesforceMarketingCloud.deleteContact configKey="OSCON"&gt;
